<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32966" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orgănĭcus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀργανικός</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>relating to
			implements</i>, <i>mechanical</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">telarum organica administratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					10, 1, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to
				musical-instruments</i>, <i>instrumental</i>, <i>musical</i>: alterum (melos), quod vocant
			organicon, Cato ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 77,
			9</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orgănĭcus</span></b> , i,
				m., <i>a musician</i>, <i><span class="en">Lucr. 5,
			334</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 132</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">2, 412</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
